CVE-2025-15366, gh-143921: imaplib rejects NUL, CR and LF in the arguments of a
command: a CR or LF of an argument ended the command and the rest went to the
server as another IMAP command. Upstream: main 6262704b134d (GH-143922) and
d0921efb665a (GH-153067, the check narrowed to NUL, CR and LF), 3.13 71926d943c
(GH-153287) and 3.14 (GH-153137); no release of 3.12 has it, its backport
(python/cpython#162135) is open on 26.11.2026. The lines of Lib/imaplib.py of
71926d943c; 3.12 has no quoting of the arguments (3.13 has), so the comment says
that the other control characters go as they are.

--- a/Lib/imaplib.py
+++ b/Lib/imaplib.py
@@ -132,6 +132,9 @@
 # We compile these in _mode_xxx.
 _Literal = br'.*{(?P<size>\d+)}$'
 _Untagged_status = br'\* (?P<data>\d+) (?P<type>[A-Z-]+)( (?P<data2>.*))?'
+# Only NUL, CR and LF are unsafe: they end the command (CVE-2025-15366);
+# the other control characters go as they are (3.12 does not quote).
+_control_chars = re.compile(b'[\x00\r\n]')
 
 
 
@@ -994,6 +997,8 @@
             if arg is None: continue
             if isinstance(arg, str):
                 arg = bytes(arg, self._encoding)
+            if _control_chars.search(arg):
+                raise ValueError("NUL, CR and LF not allowed in commands")
             data = data + b' ' + arg
 
         literal = self.literal
